#0:0
messages "Ethereal Cashimor**Subj: Re: MazeDate: May 27I had several different ideas concerning a maze of doors. Some of them mightbe workable, some impossible, but I'll make a list for you here. I don'tthink I'll implement them myself and I haven't got a finished solution...Here it comes...1) The general idea about doors: they have locks. You can hide keys behind\\   other doors and make a nice maze in the meantime...2) The idea of the well: when you open one door, another one won't open. In   combination of one way doors or doors at different distances from each   other this forces the players to cooperate in the maze.3) Doors can be trapped. When you try to unlock or picklock a door the trap   will spring, leaving the player with less hits, a terrible curse or some   thing like that...4) The nice idea of doors closing when you open one. This way the maze can   get quite confusing. Open this door, and 5 others close and can't be   opened. Very nice...   This is very interesting with two players in the maze. If one opens a door   the other sees one close again...5) Timed doors. Doors that only open one minute each five minutes. Or close   after a while. Time can make it very complicated.6) And look for another example of an interesting door to my gate in the   objects directory. This is not really something for a maze, but just the   same. I have to give it another side though...7) The most terrible of all: a door that walks through the maze of doors. A   special gate that looks like the others but replaces them sometimes. With   a special command (for example: put it into the info and use a scroll of   identify, if we have one) you can check if a door isn't the wrong one...A lot of fun, anyway. I hope I have given some ideas...Greetings from Cashimor...**Ethereal Cashimor**Subj: LanguagesDate: Jul 21Hi Herp!I thought I saw something in the race/master that has to do with languages,and I saw some naming with it. I don't know if it's going to be implemented,but I don't think the names are very well. They are a mixture of TolkienEnglish (elven), English (dwarfish, orcish, trollish) and Quenya (westron).I think we must choose ONE of these possibilities (preferable Quenya, butyou may choose any other of course)Tolkien English:human -> humanelven -> elvishwestron -> hobbitishdwarfish -> dwarvishorcish -> orcishtrollish -> trollishEnglish:human -> humanelven -> elfishwestron -> hobbitishdwarfish -> dwarfishorcish -> orcishtrollish -> trollishQuenya:human -> westronelven -> bethleur/sindarin/quenya (one of these three)westron -> kudukdwarfish -> khuzdulorcish -> orcish/morbeth (one of these two)trollish -> orcish/morbeth (one of these two)Hope to be of service with this. There are more language names in Quenya,and I'm glad to give them all to you if you want to.Greetings,Ethereal Cashimor**Ethereal Cashimor**Subj: LanguagesDate: Jul 29Here is the, still incomplete list, of languages by Tolkien or ICE:Khuzdul : DwarvesUmitic  : Half-dwarvesBethleur: Wood elvesSindarin: Grey elvesQuenya  : High/Deep/Fair elvesWestron : CommonAdunaic : High manMorbeth : Trolls/OrcsOrcish  : OrcsWaildyth: AnimalsPukael  : Wood menKuduk   : HobbitsRohirric: Horse menThere are many more languages, but I again forgot the book. Thought you mightbe interested now, since I'll be only on the MUD sporadically from now on.(Till september or something)Bye,Ethereal Cashimor**widar**To: herpSubj: Go ProblemeCc: WidarDate: Nov  4Hallo Gott! Wie angekuendigt schick ich Dir die ersten Go Probleme: .O.OOOO.....O.@@@O...O.@O.@O...O@@O@@O....@.O@OO.. How does black play so his stones will live?(@ is black).Answer: D 4Schwieigkeit: Etwas leichter als das 3. Standard-Problem.Ich muss fuer heute gehen. Waere nett wenn Du das Problem installierenkoenntest.Beste Gruesse -- Widar**widar**To: herpSubj: Go ProblemCc: widarDate: Nov  5Hi Herp! Hier das naechste Problem:  abcde1......O.O.3@@O..4.@@O.5..@O.6..@O.7@@.O.8OOO..9..... WHite (`O`) plays Black ('@') dies.Comment: This is the basic 5 point nakade shape.Answer: a5 I think I forgot the number in first column of line 2; insert itDifficulty: Kyu 24The Go ratings in Go are in Kyu with the lower number the better. A beginnerhas about kyu 30 and after about 15 games practice you are usually aroundKyu 15 (I guess). The standard problems have about the following difficulty:-  Problem 1: Kyu 29- Problem 2: Kyu 26- Problem 3: Kyu 22 I hope that helps. -- Widar, the Go Master**widar**To: herpSubj: Yet another Go ProblemCc: widarDate: Nov 10Hi Herp! Hier das Go Problem zum Tag: 1..........2....@@@@..3...@.OOO@.4...@O..O@.5..@OOO@O@.6..@O@@.@.. abcdefghij White (`O`) to play and live (1 move).Hint: By using the oiotoshi technique, you can secure life for the white stones.Solution: g4Difficulty: Kyu 21 Have Fun with this one! Don't you want to learn Go yourself :) -- Widar**widar**To: herpSubj: Go ProblemCc: widarDate: Nov 18Hi GOD! Ich hab gesehn, dass noch keine Probleme implementiert sind. WirstDu Dich mal dazusetzen oder an einen anderen Wiz weiterleiten? Auf jeden Fall, hier ist ein neues Go Problem: 7...@@@@@...6..@.OOOO@..5..@O..@O@..4..@O..O.@..3..@@OO@@...2........... ----------- abcdefghijk Black plays White ('O') dies.Black is going to have to sacrifice three stones in order to kill White.Difficulty: 21.KyuAnswer: f5 Bis zum naechsten Mal! -- Widar**widar**To: herpSubj: Go ProblemCc: widarDate: Nov 24Hi Herp! The master of all Go Problems is here again :) Here is a slightly more difficult problem:   abcdef  ------1|.O@...2|.O@...3|O@@.@.4|.OO@.5|.O.O@.6|OOOO@.7|@@@@..8|...... Comment: Black plays White (`O`) dies (3 moves). Kill all the white stones.Answer: 1) Black: a4; 2) White: a5; 3) Black: a2.        Black sacrifices two stones and by that Whites dies as he can't get two eyes       any more.       Note: 1) Black: a2; 2) White: a4. This is wrong for Black as now White has two            eyes (one at c5 and the other at a5) and can't be killed.Difficulty: Kyu 19 And as I'm just online now, waiting to regen as fighter :) here is another one: abcdef------....@.|1...@O.|2.@.@O@|3..@O.O|4..@OOO|5...@@.|6......|7....@.|8......|9 Comment: Black plays White(`O`) dies (3 moves).         If you sacrifice the black stone in atari in the right way, you can kill         the white group.Answer: 1) Black: f2; 2) White: f1; 3) Black: f2.       Black sacrifices two stones. After white 2, black retakes at f2 with 3. White is       left with only one eye and dies.       Note: Black 1 at f6 lets white capture f2, leaving him with two perfect eyes and             hence white lives.Difficulty: Kyu 19 Ok, that's it for today. Please mail me as soon as you have implemented some problems. I want to have a look at it. Bye! -- Widar  (sometimes meditating about Go)**kaz**To: patienceSubj: wiz levelsCc: herpDate: Jan 25Wiz levels:Apprentice - Level 30.	Recommended to be left for 1 week at this level to enable themto have time to read the doc files and guidelines. Also they shouldapply to a lvl 40+ for a sponsorship. (* sponsorship will be explainedbelow*) who will, at the end of the week, want to be sent mail detailinghow to 	a: Code a basic room with one monster and a few items to	   look at.	b: Code a room with at least one add_action in it.	c: Code a room with a variable number of monsters with 	   Variable statistics.	and also will want to ask a few questions on the docs and on theguidelines to ensure a good understanding of the above.	If a wizard breaks the rules, then they shall be demoted to thislevel again. They will have to stay here for at least a fortnight beforereapplying for sponsorship. If they break the rules twice they will be demoted to a newbie.	Apprentices cannot be killed, but they also cannot code, clone ormove objects about. They can teleport and echoall and emoteall.Wiz - Level 31.	At this level, they should be able to code a castle. Any problemsthey have, if they cant find an answer in the docs,k they should askeither their sponsor or other wizards, or a senior, arch or god.Senior - Level 40.	To obtain this level the wizard must have either done somethingimportant for the adminsitration of the mud, or built a quest. Whicheverit is they should then have posted a note on the notice board, and thenall wizards can say whether they approve or dissapprove of the promotionand why. If the promotion gets approval then the wizard is promoted. Atthis level, the wizard should be concentrating a little less on straightcoding and more on helping lower wizards with coding problems, and bughunting/solving. They should have full read access and partial writeaccess (* all except player.o files and obvious ones like player.c etc *)If you have sponsored someone, then YOU are responsible for them and whatthey code. If it breaks the guidlelines you have to tell them to fix it.If it dosent, demote them to a level 30.Arch - Level  50.	An arch is the top trouble shooter for debugging and codingproblems. They should have full read/write access to enable this. In short, they have to do approximately the same job as a senior except with more bug hunting and less personal coding, and more powers to workwith.God - Level 51+.	Pretty self explanatory.General rules:	No player helping/hindrance. 	If a player comes to you and tells you that they got killed by a bug, you order them to mail an arch or god about it. Let the archesor gods sort that one out, its not your problem.	If you want to test an area, use either the test character or apersonal secondary character. DO NOT use players for this.	Do not open partly finished areas/quests.	Do not create super weapons or armours. Quest items are allowedto be a little more powerful but not excessively so.	Do not go around healing players. Thats helping them, and it takes away from the actual game itself.	REMINDER: Breaking the above rules once means demotion to		  a level 30. Breaking them twice means being demoted		  to a level 1.Please reply to me about what you think of this and the monster stats.One last thing about the wizard levels. You could make it that certainarches are in charge of certain parts of coding, i.e. quests,monsters, players, rooms, special functions etc.**ouzo**To: herpSubj: hi du arschfickerDate: Mar 19Hi !wenn ich lust und laune hab,werd ich dir dein dummes mud abdrehen wixer !!             Laugh *** whisky the god **tony**To: herpSubj: prisonDate: May  6Someone imprisoned my batman character for no reason.Can you free it please?Anthony**animal**To: herpSubj: CheatingDate: May  7Hmmm, it seems someone is cheating with my quest.....I noticed NO ONE killed the King to get his head...BUT line 652 shows Carefree throwing the head.......Look at /players/animal/quest    There is NO WAY to get the headunless 1) you kill the King, or 2) a wiz clones it....Please check into it..I guess I should make the head clone proof....AnimalP.S.  Any suggestions?**airborne**To: herpSubj: Memory conservation...Date: May  8As James suggested in the /room/adv_inner board, /room/* rooms need to be updand i will volunteer to do it if you wish to grant me temporary write access to files in that directory.Later man.Airborne.**animal**To: herp Re:   cheatingDate: May  9I will add the log_file in reset when callked with a 0, no problem.I will log it to AN in /log if thats ok with you? orif you want it somewhere else, please tell me thanks :-)Animal**colossus**To: herpSubj: sheriffDate: May 14Hi Herp, I'd like to ask if it was possible for me to apply for thepost of sheriff. I