f that you have here, so they canadd it to their mud. They run Amylaar parser too, apparently...letr me know if its OK to give the stuff to em, and what they need besides thefiles in /udp  -James**james**To: herpSubj: clone_objectCc: llort patience kbl jamesDate: May 27I added a simul_efun for clone_object, that checks to see if the previousobject is a non-cloned monster. IE, if someone defines a monster byinheriting monster.c, i will detect all the original loaded objects ofthis type. All such objects are logged in /log/BAD_CLONE_OBJECT , thoughthe clone_object is still allowed to proceed as normal.Now, alot of unnecessary cloning of armor, weapons, money, etc is doneby the original monster objects, when in reality all that we usually wantis for the clones of these monsters to be cloning equipment. So, should we try to have the simul_efun refuse to clone objects in this case (actually, we would probably need to return some dummy  object pointerinstead of returning a value of 0)...OR, should we have the simul_efun ofclone_object() log the error message to the error log of the wizard whoowns the monster, and make them add a check to each monster?  -James**kbl**To: herpSubj: YesDate: May 27Ok, what I take it as, we do not want the, ie: elf.c file to inside it cloneitems, instead we would like it to be cloned, then clone items and transferthen to the elf... so we are not cloning inside of a cloned object. Thatswhat I got out of that, sounds resonable to me, less recursive cloning.Is that what YOU thought it said, or did I read it wrong, and I read itseveral times to get it straight.                                                        Kblps: How did your final come out?? Good I bet! :)**james**To: herp Re:   simul_efun::clone_objectDate: May 29Ah, but i'm calling query_npc() in each object, so i'm only dealing withmaster objects that are monsters... There shouldnt be any master-objectsthat are monsters in the game, that need to clone other objects... Theonly master-object-monster that comes to mind is /obj/shut.c (Armageddon),and i dont think thats considered an NPC, but if it is, i know itdoesnt need to clone armor and weapons...  -James**james**To: herpSubj: udp portDate: Jun  7what is our udp port?**matt**To: patienceSubj: There's no place like homeCc: herp llort cashimorDate: Jun 11Hello.	I just want to tell you that I don't want to have to leave this mud.I love it here, it's like home to me since I've been playing for so long.It's just that when such drastic changes occur in a short time, changes whichare not at all discussed with other wizzes let alone players, it upsets me.For instance the new name information. The insertion of the race in the middleof their title disturbs the flow of titles; they don't sound as good.Also the \"is standing here\" and \"is here\" appended to the end of objects in aroom isn't necessary, especially for items which have a special short namewhich isn't compatible (i.e. doesn't sound right) with \"is here\" appended.If a wiz wants the object to have \"is here\" he can just add that to the shortdesc of the object. It shouldn't be mandatory.	The changes to \"who\" are excellent. I like the new who command. But Ithink that if you took out the race from the titles, and instead made a\"who <race>\" command or some such thing, that would be better. Races can geta list of their members already, after all, by typing \"race\".	I have more suggestions and opinions which I do not have space toinclude here. Please read my note on the inner adv. board about the meeting,for I would like to discuss things with you, and not have to leave HM.	Greetings, 	Matt**matt**To: herpSubj: What will happen now ?Date: Jun 12Hello. Now that patience has banished himself and llort has left the mud,who will fix was has been disturbed? There are still many bugs ... playersseem to want the mud back to the 