him guildmaster of thieves. Now I don't know what he may have told you, but Iwill tell you what I've said to him:One day he asked me whether he could become guildmaster of thieves.At that point, I had mentioned to him several reasons why I would notdo so:1) Thieves is a rather ok guild that works like fine. 2) When the skill system is coming (which will be in a week now, I hope),   there will be a lot of things to reconsider, among which appointing   new guildmasters.3) Given these points it would only cause players to whine when they're   new abilities one day, and take them back the next coz of changes.   All we want now is a stable, well running mud.4) There were other people that had asked for the job, which I could   have given it before. For those same reasons, I did not.So now I don't think Kasgaroth had the right to come to you 'asking' forthe job. I was purposely not looking for a new guildmaster, and he knew.Apart from that, I don't like his note on thief board (nr 22), statingthat their GM is gone and that they should now go complaining for a newone. Of course you will cause players to start whining that way.So now you know the story from this side, I wanted to ask you if it's okwith you to remove Kasgaroth as guildmaster of thieves (running it fromyour dirs again, leaderless). At the appropriate time I will reconsiderthe matter, in conference with the arches. I understand you put someoneyou think would do well to look after your guild, but as arch of guilds,I don't think it all too wise. Please let me know what you think of this.See you around (:-),			Viking Lord UglymouthP.S. There's ye olle rule, which you made and I still think in general a     wise one, that says that players may not take over the guild to which     they belonged when they were still mortals. Think it over...  :-)					Uglymouth**eponine**To: herpSubj: oh andDate: Mar 31if i'm not here, i've gone to my acct, eponine@phantom.com**widar