hat situation.As said, last remarks are on personal basis. I would like to get youropinions on the matter, so we can come to a final decision, and stickto that decision together. The arches must be on one line if things areto work properly here. At least on such matters, I think.See you around,				Viking Lord Uglymouth**wesley**To: herpSubj: Manchester addressesDate: Jun  6uk.ac.umist.cn.pad: umist PAD.cn.xa: reverse PAD.cns: central services sun.co.ap: apollo cluster.co.ist: info systems tech lab 2.co.mac: Macintosh gateway.co.mp: sun 600 series.csc: control systems centre mail computer.dir: umist dir server**uglymouth**To: matt Re:   re: promotion to newwizCc: galadriel,herp,airborne,warlord,silas,cashimorDate: Jun 14Hi,Thanks for mail, Matt.Well, as I also discussed with Airborne (and now from yourmail as well), I think we mostly agree on how things shouldbe done. I plan to write a doc soon on this practice (who isallowed, and what should be tested), which you then can commenton. If ok, then I'll take it up in the docs.So, I guess we all agree on the fact that only arches shouldtake the final test. I don't mind having mentors taking preliminarytests, but it should be clear to the appr that it's only just that.Whatever way mentors and students like to work is completely up tothem, as far as I'm concerned. For us it's the result that counts.Another important point you mention is that the test is not onlya test of knowledge, but also a good opportunity to plug up someholes in the apprs knowledge, and explain other things you as archthink are important for the soon-to-be-newwiz to know. Also, I letthem ask any question they want to ask, or tell me when somethingI say is not entirely clear to them. It benefits the newwiz, andalso gives a much more relaxed tone to the test, and is I think agood way to show them that the arches aren't as bad and egocentricas they are stereotypically portraited ;-)I'll write the doc, and let you all know when it's finished, sowe can make the decision public knowledge, for all to adhere to.See you around,			Viking Lord Uglymouth**cashimor**To: herpSubj: Current balance of powerDate: Nov 10Dear Herp,There are a few problems, both in real life and here, that make it impossiblefor me to continue working as arch-wizard for you for a while. I herebyrequest demotion to 'retired' for at least one month, maybe longer,depending on circumstances. My reasons are as follows:1) I'm quite busy in real life, examinations and a big project.2) The current power-management in this MUD is unsatisfactory to me.   The way Muzmuz banishes people with childish reasons,   and Llort comes in and simply says 'no' to everything I do   make it rather hard to function.I hope that you appreciate the work I've done in the short time that I wasan arch-wizard. I still want to implement the skill-system or try to makebetter solutions for all those auto_load weapons that are currently availablebut since the majority is against such changes (they prefer power above playability it seems) I will not go against them.Greetings,Ethereal CashimorP.S. I will still visit this place regularly though. I still feel this is my     home.**mangla**To: herpSubj: badfile nameDate: Dec 28/players/tamina/teds/hot   there is a filenamethat has a backspace char as its name.-Mangla**dice**To: airborneSubj: Guild ArchCc: muzmuz herp llort mangla silasDate: Feb  3OlaI read Tatsuos mail applying for guild arch,And i don't think he's fit for that job, He's too powerhungry, and still looking for more powerAt the time he had access to the ninja-guild he screwed around royallynot allowing players to join the guild for he didn't like themraising the -san level again for he didn't want a certain player to become a sanSo he should not become guild-arch in my opinionIf a guild arch is needed, be careful who you choose/Dice**blaarg*